title: Handle relay v3→v2 scheduling rollback for v3-capable parachains

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      If the relay chain rolls back the `CandidateReceiptV3` node feature, a v3-capable parachain
      falls back to v2 candidates instead of stalling. "V3 active" is derived dynamically from the
      para constant and the relay feature read from the committed state proof — the inherent and
      `validate_block` read the same entry, so author and PVF cannot disagree. On the fallback,
      `validate_block` accepts the v2 candidate and the inherent keeps the relay-parent-descendant
      check active. The bound on the `CoreInfo` digest's `claim_queue_offset` now allows the widest
      lookup either scheduling version can make, `V3_CLAIM_QUEUE_LOOKAHEAD + relay_parent_offset`,
      so a collator whose view of the para runtime lags by a block cannot stall the chain. Reading
      `node_features` goes via a new decode-only `RelayHostConfigurationPrefix`.
crates:
  - name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
    bump: minor
  - name: polkadot-primitives
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-primitives-core
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-test-relay-sproof-builder
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
    bump: none
